---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Government Operations & Transparency | Phil Burney for Commissioner"
  description="Phil Burney's platform on open, accountable government for Rutherford County District 5."
>
  <section class="section platform-hero">
    <p class="tag">Platform</p>
    <h1>Government Operations &amp; Transparency</h1>
    <p class="muted lead">
      Good government starts with honesty. Phil believes every resident has a right to
      know how their county is run, who is making decisions, and why. Accountability
      isn't optional — it's the foundation of public trust.
    </p>
    <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline back-link">← All Platform Issues</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section platform-stack">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Open Meetings &amp; Public Records</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        County business belongs to the public. Phil will ensure that commission meetings
        are fully accessible, agendas are posted in advance, and public records requests
        are fulfilled promptly and completely.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Post meeting agendas and supporting documents at least 72 hours in advance</li>
        <li>Livestream and archive all commission and committee meetings online</li>
        <li>Enforce timely compliance with North Carolina public records law</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Ethical Government &amp; Conflict of Interest</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Elected officials must serve the public, not personal or financial interests.
        Phil will push for clear ethics standards and real enforcement so residents
        can trust the decisions being made on their behalf.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Require commissioners to disclose financial interests related to county votes</li>
        <li>Strengthen conflict-of-interest recusal policies and enforce them consistently</li>
        <li>Support an independent ethics review process for county officials</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Efficient County Operations</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Residents deserve a county government that works efficiently and treats their
        time as valuable. Phil will push for streamlined permitting, responsive
        departments, and services that are easy to access.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Set and publish service response-time standards for county departments</li>
        <li>Modernize permitting and licensing processes to reduce unnecessary delays</li>
        <li>Conduct regular audits of county operations to identify waste and inefficiency</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Citizen Engagement</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The people most affected by local decisions should have a real voice in making
        them. Phil is committed to making county government approachable, responsive,
        and genuinely connected to the communities it serves.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hold regular district town halls to hear directly from residents</li>
        <li>Expand public comment opportunities before major votes</li>
        <li>Create a clear, accessible way for constituents to track commissioner actions</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Hold your government accountable</h2>
      <p>Phil is committed to earning and keeping your trust. Help him bring open, honest leadership to District 5.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/donations" class="btn btn-primary">Support the Campaign</a>
        <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline-light">View All Issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .platform-hero {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .platform-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .back-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
  }
</style>
